  "reference": "O/E funnel centered on the risk model itself (cl=1.0) rather than on the pooled SMR, same data as funnel_oe_exact. This is the benchmarking form: it asks who differs from their model-expected count, where the default pooled center line asks who differs from their peers and so absorbs any overall miscalibration of the expected-events model. Limits recenter on lambda = 1.0*E, narrowing slightly (first point ucl 3.665015 vs 3.717113) because the cohort runs 1.7% above expected. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
